   $q$"She told herself she was only resting her hands." What does this sentence reveal about Noor?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is bored by the note and is waiting politely for him to turn the screen back.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She is trying to hide from Mr. Abernathy that she has stopped working entirely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She is physically worn out from typing nine pages and needs a long break.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She is becoming interested in the note but is reluctant to admit it to herself.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She is becoming interested in the note but is reluctant to admit it to herself.$q$, $q$"Told herself" signals an excuse; she "looked at it longer than she meant to" because the note has caught her interest, which clashes with her pride in speed. Reading it as simple tiredness takes the excuse at face value.$q$, 'draft', 'ad335b15-aa6a-592a-96df-74695b05d564')
