-- Passage rg10-character-setting-plot-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ffec356f-cab5-57b8-a052-9c859ab56621', 'rg10-character-setting-plot-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Eight Seconds$q$, $q$Coach Petrakis waited until the team bus was pulling into the conference course before she sat down beside Marisol Okada. "I need you to run the first two miles with Hana," she said. "She goes out too fast and dies on the big hill. If she finishes in the top twenty, we win the meet."

Marisol nodded because that was what captains did, but her stomach tightened. She had trained all season to break twenty minutes, and this flat, fast course was her last real chance before winter. Running with a freshman for two miles meant giving that chance away.

She also remembered, sharply and unwillingly, her own first conference race, when she had sprinted the opening half mile and then walked the hill in tears while a senior named Tova jogged back to run beside her.

At the gun, Hana shot forward. Marisol caught her elbow lightly. "Not yet," she said. "Stay on my shoulder." Through the first mile Hana kept glancing at the runners ahead, and Marisol kept talking: about breathing, about the shade at the turn, about anything except the watch on her own wrist, which she refused to look at.

On the hill, Hana's breath went ragged. Marisol shortened her stride and counted steps aloud until they crested together. At the two-mile marker Hana gasped, "Go. I'm okay now." Marisol hesitated for one step, then ran.

She crossed the line in 20:08. She stared at the numbers for a long time. Then the results went up on the board: Hana, eighteenth, and the team, first by four points. Hana found her in the crowd and hugged her so hard they both nearly fell.

Marisol hugged her back. The eight seconds still stung, and she let them sting. She was surprised to find that the other feeling was just as large.$q$, 'draft')
