   $q$In the final paragraph, "The eight seconds still stung, and she let them sting. She was surprised to find that the other feeling was just as large." What does this ending show about Marisol's development?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is mainly relieved that the race is over and has no strong feelings about the result.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"She regrets helping Hana and plans to run only for herself at every future meet this season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character-change"},{"text":"She has decided that personal goals are selfish, so she no longer cares about her time at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She holds both disappointment and pride at once, accepting a real cost for the team without pretending it is gone.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She holds both disappointment and pride at once, accepting a real cost for the team without pretending it is gone.$q$, $q$She "let them sting" yet finds "the other feeling," her joy in the team's win and Hana's race, "just as large," so both motives remain. The choice saying she no longer cares about her time is tempting but ignores that the time still stings.$q$, 'draft', 'ffec356f-cab5-57b8-a052-9c859ab56621')
