-- Passage rg10-character-setting-plot-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('94d714ad-1d2b-5673-adb0-305456ae689a', 'rg10-character-setting-plot-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Eleven Lines$q$, $q$The weather station on the roof of the Raman apartment building had worked for exactly three days before its humidity readings went wild, jumping from forty percent to ninety and back within a minute. Priya Raman spent a week rewiring the sensor and got nowhere. Her cousin Teo, who was twelve and visited on Sundays, looked at her screen for twenty minutes, then wrote eleven lines of code that averaged each reading against the ones before it. The numbers settled down like a dog that had finally been told to sit.

Now the station had a website, a live graph, and a spot in the district technology showcase. The showcase was open only to high school students, and the entry form had one line for the student's name and another for "Additional contributors (optional)."

Priya wanted to win. The winner received a summer internship at a university engineering lab, which would look excellent on her applications, and she had built nearly everything herself. Nearly. She left the second line blank, then filled it in, then deleted it again.

"You can leave me off," Teo said that Sunday, when she finally told him about the form. "I'm not even old enough to enter." He said it lightly, but he went back to his game a little too quickly.

Her teacher, Mr. Castellanos, read her draft poster the following week. "Judges like projects that are clearly the student's own work," he said carefully. "You might not want a big credit line for someone else."

Priya thought about the eleven lines of code, and about how the graph had looked before them. She printed a new poster. Under the title, in letters exactly as tall as her own name, it said: Data smoothing code by Teodoro Raman, age 12.

When the judges reached her table, the first question they asked was who Teodoro was. Priya smiled and told them.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
