   $q$Teo says "You can leave me off," but "he went back to his game a little too quickly." What does this suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Teo is embarrassed that his code did not actually fix the humidity readings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Teo is angry at Priya and plans to enter the showcase with his own project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Teo is hurt but is hiding it, which adds weight to Priya's decision.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Teo truly does not care about the project and is more interested in his game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Teo is hurt but is hiding it, which adds weight to Priya's decision.$q$, $q$"A little too quickly" signals that his light tone covers disappointment, which makes leaving him off harder for Priya. Taking his words at face value misses that signal.$q$, 'draft', '94d714ad-1d2b-5673-adb0-305456ae689a')
