   $q$How does the release in Text 2 differ from the string snapping in Text 1?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In both texts the release happens by accident during a sudden gust of wind on a hill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"In Text 2 letting go is an accident, while in Text 1 the girl decides to cut the string on purpose.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"In both texts the released object falls quickly and is damaged when it lands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"In Text 2 letting go is a planned choice, while in Text 1 it is an accident that the kite welcomes.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In Text 2 letting go is a planned choice, while in Text 1 it is an accident that the kite welcomes.$q$, $q$The kite's string "snapped" on a gusty afternoon, while Yusra "opened her hand" after months of preparation. The payload lands where the beacon predicted, so it is not ruined like the kite.$q$, 'draft', '59b3cd2c-92ca-524f-9823-2f13b7c6d076')
