   $q$How does Text 2 change the way the keeper's value is recognized?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In the myth the keeper is chosen by chance, but in Text 2 she wins a formal contest against the motor.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"In both texts the keeper is chosen right away because everyone already admires her patience.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-transformation"},{"text":"In the myth a test reveals the best keeper, but in Text 2 her value appears only after the replacement fails and her records are shown.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In the myth the keeper is rejected at first, but in Text 2 the council praises her from the start.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In the myth a test reveals the best keeper, but in Text 2 her value appears only after the replacement fails and her records are shown.$q$, $q$The animals test all three candidates before choosing, while the council cheers the motor and changes course only after it fails and Theo brings the notebooks. The council does not admire her from the start, so the "chosen right away" choice is wrong.$q$, 'draft', 'ff8b5c12-6e50-5a5a-b4b8-08011d52b932')
