   $q$How does the author connect the telegraph to the spread of railway time?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The telegraph let each town send its own local time to every other station.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"The telegraph was built because the national law of 1874 required a single time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The telegraph made railway time easy to check, so more and more groups adopted it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The telegraph replaced the railway, so towns no longer needed a shared timetable.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The telegraph made railway time easy to check, so more and more groups adopted it.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 says that "once railway time could be checked so easily," banks, schools and councils adopted it. The telegraph came in 1860, years before the 1874 law, so it could not have been built because of that law.$q$, 'draft', 'bc864218-4c8c-52e6-bde0-588203f3f66e')
