   $q$The word "scored" has several meanings. In paragraph 2, the plows "scored the surface in a grid." Which meaning fits this context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"earned points in a contest","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"wrote music for an orchestra","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"marked with cut lines or grooves","is_correct":true},{"text":"melted with heat and pressure","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$marked with cut lines or grooves$q$, $q$The same sentence says the plows were "carving long grooves that guided the workers," so scored means marked with cut lines. Earning points is the most familiar meaning of the word, but ice crews cutting blocks are not competing in a game.$q$, 'draft', 'f8a6ef5e-e307-5209-a671-71b62019a896')
