   $q$Achterberg's comments in the last paragraph suggest which conclusion about the results?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The guide probably helped, but the size of the drop may be somewhat overstated.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The results are meaningless because families likely made up their logs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"},{"text":"The first survey was less reliable than the second because it was shorter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The second survey proves the guide works and should be used in every town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-limitations"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The guide probably helped, but the size of the drop may be somewhat overstated.$q$, $q$Achterberg notes that honest recording and families knowing "they were being watched" could affect the numbers, which questions the size of the effect without dismissing it. He never says families invented their logs, so "meaningless" goes beyond the text.$q$, 'draft', '302f1042-d238-54e1-9bc9-79b37baae6d8')
