   $q$Tobias tells himself he was "not slow" but "only careful." Why does he prefer the word "careful"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Careful\" and \"slow\" mean exactly the same thing, so the choice does not matter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"},{"text":"\"Careful\" means he played faster than Priya did in the opening.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"\"Careful\" frames his long thinking as a strength, while \"slow\" sounds like a weakness.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Careful\" describes the way he handled the wooden pieces with his hands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Careful" frames his long thinking as a strength, while "slow" sounds like a weakness.$q$, $q$Both words can describe taking a long time, but "careful" carries a positive connotation of thoughtfulness, which is why Tobias "told himself" to use it. He clearly did not play faster, since Priya moved "in the first minute."$q$, 'draft', '248dda41-945b-504d-807d-6115bfb9063e')
