   $q$What does the oxymoron "controlled fall" suggest about the demonstrations?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The platform never moved at all once the rope had been cut.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The assistant slowly lowered the platform with a second rope.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The platform really dropped, but the brake kept the drop safe and limited.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The crowd controlled the event by deciding when the rope was cut.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The platform really dropped, but the brake kept the drop safe and limited.$q$, $q$The author defines it as "a drop that was frightening but never truly dangerous," and the platform "would lurch, and then it would hold." It did move, so saying it never moved contradicts the lurch.$q$, 'draft', '2462c730-093c-517d-8801-94b1d288a8d5')
