   $q$Mrs. Halvorsen describes the instrument as "a piano with a lot of history." What does this euphemism really mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The piano once belonged to a famous musician from long ago.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The piano came with a book about the history of music.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The piano was brand new and had never been played before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The piano was old and worn, with several problems that needed fixing.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The piano was old and worn, with several problems that needed fixing.$q$, $q$The next paragraph reveals what "history" meant: a wobbly leg, missing key tops and buzzing low notes. Nothing in the passage mentions a famous owner, so that reading adds information the text does not give.$q$, 'draft', '55e04f37-dcb7-5914-9a5b-d7401c418c67')
