   $q$According to the passage, what does a bike with "character" most likely have?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A famous previous owner who rode it in races.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A cartoon character painted on the frame.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Visible wear such as scratched paint and a squeaky chain.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Brand new parts that were installed last week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Visible wear such as scratched paint and a squeaky chain.$q$, $q$The author translates the euphemism directly: a bike with "character" may have "scratched paint and a squeaky chain." Reading "character" as a painted figure takes the word literally and misses the euphemism.$q$, 'draft', '5881a7d5-59e2-52c6-94a7-1ea9049b07d8')
