   $q$The author says sellers "speak a language of their own." What does this phrase mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Most bicycle sellers speak a foreign language instead of English.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Sellers refuse to answer any questions that buyers ask them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Sellers write listings that are completely impossible to read.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-extreme"},{"text":"Sellers use special phrases whose real meanings a buyer has to figure out.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sellers use special phrases whose real meanings a buyer has to figure out.$q$, $q$The next sentence says a buyer must "translate it," and the passage then explains phrases like "gently used." The listings can be read; they just need interpreting, so "impossible to read" goes too far.$q$, 'draft', '5881a7d5-59e2-52c6-94a7-1ea9049b07d8')
