values
  ('8c3feae2-e5c7-5d42-bd2e-d784fce60c44', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Ifeoma calls the rehearsal "organized chaos." What does this oxymoron suggest about the scene?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rehearsal was perfectly calm and quiet from start to finish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The room looked wild and messy, yet a plan was still guiding the work.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The cast had organized a party instead of holding a rehearsal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Nobody knew what they were doing, and the rehearsal had no plan.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-extreme"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The room looked wild and messy, yet a plan was still guiding the work.$q$, $q$The actors wandering and the thunder effect show chaos, while Ifeoma's cue sheet and headset show organization: "When she spoke into the headset, the crew moved." Saying nobody had a plan ignores the "organized" half of the phrase.$q$, 'draft', '621ead57-d96b-532a-8dc5-8ef6ef0fc115')
