   $q$Ifeoma tells the cast, "We are experiencing a brief intermission." Why does she use this euphemism instead of saying the board is broken?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She truly believes the play was scheduled to take a break at that point.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She wants to keep the cast calm by making a frustrating problem sound like a planned pause.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She wants to blame Hana publicly for causing the lights to fail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"She does not yet know that anything has gone wrong in the booth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She wants to keep the cast calm by making a frustrating problem sound like a planned pause.$q$, $q$She speaks "calmly," and the result is that "the tension in the room loosened," which shows the euphemism was meant to reassure. The stage had gone dark mid-scene, so she clearly knew something was wrong.$q$, 'draft', '621ead57-d96b-532a-8dc5-8ef6ef0fc115')
