   $q$Why does the author begin the story with the cracked vase already on display at the exhibition?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To make readers curious about how the vase cracked and why it is still being shown","is_correct":true},{"text":"To prove that the visitors in the gallery were the ones who broke the vase","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To show that Nadia has already decided to quit making glass after the exhibition","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To explain the cobalt glassblowing process before the main events of the story","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To make readers curious about how the vase cracked and why it is still being shown$q$, $q$Opening on the finished, cracked vase raises questions (how did it crack, why display it) that the flashback then answers. Nothing suggests visitors broke it; the man's guess is later corrected by the card.$q$, 'draft', '1a270ac8-ac74-5c13-b42a-385aa713cf4c')
