   $q$How does the parallel structure build tension at 11:55 a.m.?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The class learns that Arun found the box, so the tension comes from whether he will return it to the school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"The class fears the box is lost just as the reader sees Arun walking toward it, so readers wait for the two lines to meet.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Arun cannot find the box in his field, so the tension comes from whether the tracker will start working again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Both sections end with the balloon still rising, so the tension comes from whether it will ever reach the ground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The class fears the box is lost just as the reader sees Arun walking toward it, so readers wait for the two lines to meet.$q$, $q$At the same minute, the tracker goes silent for Priya while Arun approaches the box, so the reader holds information the characters lack. The class has not yet learned anything about Arun.$q$, 'draft', '7cd89c4b-d65a-50e6-8683-4025c04e8e58')
