   $q$What is the effect of repeating "Before that" at the start of most stanzas?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It marks each step backward in time and gives the poem a steady, rewinding rhythm.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests the events in each stanza happened on the same day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It shows the speaker cannot remember the correct order of events.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It signals that each stanza describes a different family moving out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It marks each step backward in time and gives the poem a steady, rewinding rhythm.$q$, $q$"Before that" works like a rewind button, carrying the reader one stage earlier each time. The steady repetition shows control, not confusion, about the order.$q$, 'draft', 'dcbba9d9-b980-5112-92c2-67d4dceaf0a4')
