   $q$Which detail best shows the difference between how the narrator and her aunt think about time at the start?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The narrator's teacher hangs the strip on the wall, while the aunt keeps the finished rug.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The narrator cards wool on the first day, while the aunt cards wool on the second day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"The narrator weaves with red and gray, while the aunt prefers dyes made from sagebrush.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The narrator makes a schedule with colored blocks, while the aunt keeps no clock in her weaving room.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The narrator makes a schedule with colored blocks, while the aunt keeps no clock in her weaving room.$q$, $q$The colored-block schedule and the clockless room directly contrast a deadline mindset with a patient, unmeasured one. The colors of wool have nothing to do with time.$q$, 'draft', '66b84920-0178-539d-b1b0-048e495b9f43')
