   $q$Why does the single-sentence paragraph "Then the green jersey looked back." create tension?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Its isolation signals the end of the race, so the remaining paragraphs are a flashback.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"Its isolation marks a turning point, hinting the leader feels threatened and pushing Sun-hee into action.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Its isolation shows that the leader has stopped running, guaranteeing that Sun-hee will win.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Its isolation shows that the leader is looking for her coach, which is unrelated to Sun-hee.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Its isolation marks a turning point, hinting the leader feels threatened and pushing Sun-hee into action.$q$, $q$Setting the sentence alone breaks the calm and signals a shift; immediately after, "Sun-hee moved." The leader keeps running, and Sun-hee still finishes behind her.$q$, 'draft', 'b14140a3-74a6-52ca-8677-968b3cb4f4c0')
