  ('26fbb837-e6e3-55e2-abc2-83228bcaae27', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why does the author present the letters one at a time, in the order Teodora reads them?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reveals the writer's full name early, so the ending only confirms what readers know.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It lets the author skip the bridge's construction and focus only on the dog.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It lets the writer's story unfold gradually, so the reader grows attached along with Teodora.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the letters were sent out of order, which confuses Teodora about the dates.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It lets the writer's story unfold gradually, so the reader grows attached along with Teodora.$q$, $q$Revealing details letter by letter (bridge, dog, cold, unmet daughter) draws the reader in the same way it draws in Teodora, who "kept reading." The full name is never given.$q$, 'draft', 'ed175c7e-8e4b-554a-986e-8657ca6d97cf')
