values
  ('2e5bfaba-5af0-566d-9207-c2327b469d0f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Earlier the speaker leaves out her father's joke and his story about running a shop. How does the ending change the meaning of those omissions?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They now seem untrue, showing that the father invented the shop to impress the clerk.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They now seem like a loss, showing that in deciding what crosses she also hid who her father really is.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They now seem accidental, showing that the speaker simply forgot to translate those sentences.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They now seem wise, showing that the clerk would have been confused by too much information.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They now seem like a loss, showing that in deciding what crosses she also hid who her father really is.$q$, $q$Once the father appears capable and full of effort, the dropped joke and the forty workers read as parts of him the speaker filtered out, and "I did not ask" admits she overlooked him too. She cut them on purpose ("She does not need that, I tell myself"), so it was not forgetting.$q$, 'draft', 'ba38fac0-98d2-578f-91aa-780c67c15e31')
