   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kit houses were a brilliant idea that showed how much better life was in the early 1900s. Modern families should be able to order homes this way instead of paying for expensive builders.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Early 1900s catalog companies shipped precut house kits by rail to places without architects or skilled builders. The kits spread the same designs across many towns, had some flaws, faded by the 1940s, and many houses still stand.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In the early 1900s, families in Vellin ordered houses from catalogs. A railroad car brought numbered boards, doorknobs and window glass, and the family built the home with one experienced builder.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Lumber companies in Vellin tricked families into buying houses that fell apart in prairie winters. Historians are now finding the damaged homes by searching attics for numbered beams.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"distorts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Early 1900s catalog companies shipped precut house kits by rail to places without architects or skilled builders. The kits spread the same designs across many towns, had some flaws, faded by the 1940s, and many houses still stand.$q$, $q$The third choice gives the main points of every paragraph in neutral words. The first choice is accurate but covers only the ordering process and leaves out the kits' effects and decline.$q$, 'draft', '800edc91-6bef-5e00-aa9d-08739653e7d0')
