  ('f597aeba-f128-5450-9ab6-e725d973073c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-main-idea-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Hikers in the Ashcombe Hills carelessly ignore the ants that keep the forest alive. The invasive ants are destroying the hills, and people must act now before the hollowbell disappears forever.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Native ants and invasive ants compete for hollowbell seeds. A botanist found that the native ants plant the seeds on purpose so that more food will grow near their nests.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The hollowbell grows in the Ashcombe Hills. Its seeds have fatty attachments, and ants carry them to their nests, where they eat the attachments and feed them to their young.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Native ants carry hollowbell seeds to their nests for a fatty reward and discard the seeds in rich, hidden soil, where they sprout better. Where invasive ants have replaced native ones, the plant is declining, so its survival depends on that partnership.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Native ants carry hollowbell seeds to their nests for a fatty reward and discard the seeds in rich, hidden soil, where they sprout better. Where invasive ants have replaced native ones, the plant is declining, so its survival depends on that partnership.$q$, $q$The last choice covers how the partnership works, its benefit, the threat and the conclusion without opinions. The third choice adds a purpose the passage never states, since the ants simply discard seeds they cannot eat.$q$, 'draft', '9bb116b0-d618-5546-8e82-4d075173c889')
