   $q$Which inference about the weathervane is best supported by its final line?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It believes the kite is useless and should be thrown out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-inference"},{"text":"Its worth comes from faithfully turning with the wind, though it never leaves its place.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is pleased that the kite was ruined in the storm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It wants the farmer to thank it for saving the hay wagon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Its worth comes from faithfully turning with the wind, though it never leaves its place.$q$, $q$The weathervane grants that the kite flew higher ("You did") and then points out that its turning warned the farmer, so its value lies in its steady usefulness. Its calm agreement shows no pleasure in the kite's damage.$q$, 'draft', 'c1a1a6bd-05b3-55c3-beb0-33d8d34d3ed7')
