   $q$According to the poem, how does the grandfather start each seam?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He turns the machine's wheel by hand.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He threads a new needle for each seam.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He pins the fabric on the wooden box.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"He presses the pedal with his foot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sequence-error"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He turns the machine's wheel by hand.$q$, $q$The second stanza says the machine "has a wheel he turns by hand to start each seam." His foot finds the pedal only after that, "then," so the pedal comes second.$q$, 'draft', '37d0465c-8de8-515d-8f30-327b0ed629e5')
