   $q$What does Mrs. Ostrowski's habit of pointing at the log, instead of correcting Ravi aloud, suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She does not know the correct procedures for the contest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She wants Ravi to learn to catch his own mistakes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She is embarrassed by Ravi and wants him to stop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She is too busy eating to pay attention to the contest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She wants Ravi to learn to catch his own mistakes.$q$, $q$She points to each error so that "he would see the mistake and fix it himself," which shows she is teaching him to find errors on his own. She spots every mistake, so she is clearly paying attention.$q$, 'draft', 'a6a05ab9-b449-5c56-ae70-4422edf5b9f8')
